 "permalink": "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/10546695/do-we-need-to-explicitly-call-the-destructor-for-the-simple-pod-classes-alloca",
 "body_html": "<p>Here by \"simple\", I mean a class with non-virtual empty destructor or POD type.</p>\n\n<p>Typical example:</p>\n\n<pre><code>char buffer[SIZE];\nT *p = new(buffer) T;\n...\np-&gt;~T();  // &lt;---- always ?\n</code></pre>\n\n<p>What happens if we don't call the explicit destructor on <code>p</code>? I don't think it is undefined behavior or memory leak.<br>\nIs there any problem with reusing <code>buffer</code> ?</p>\n",
 "passes": [
